Z||000004||AusFiero||09-02-2001||03:32 AM||||From reading it's website GM has nothing to do with it. Basically it is an extremely overpriced kit car. I do not believe their $1,000,000 development costs. Look around at some other kit cars and see if they spent that much to get the same results. Nice looking yes, but definately a kit car with a good write up by a professional marketting team. Give me half that amount and I could build you the same or better. I am talking about half the $120,000 too not half a million. Wonder how many people will fall for the marketting that makes it sound like smething special. Yeah it is. But not what they are trying to make it into with marketting glitz and glamour. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||13
Z||000005||Archie||09-02-2001||07:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AusFiero:<BR><B>From reading it's website GM has nothing to do with it. Basically it is an extremely overpriced kit car. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I totally agree Jim, There is a con going on every minute. This con is brought to you by Kruse International. These auction houses want you to respect their name, then they put on mis-leading auctions like this one.<P>Archie||||reg||1
