Z||000009||Songman||09-02-2001||10:40 AM||||I think that is the VIN for the car... Look at the roofline. Looks like a Corvette rebody to me... and an 84 yet!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||California Kid||09-02-2001||12:01 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Urchin:<BR><B>That reminds me of when I had first taken an interest in fieros.  I had been told on more than one occasion that pontiac had produced a number of V8 fieros in '88 which led to them being discontinued.  According to sources the fiero was resposible for a reduction in corvette sales.  Fieros offered equal power at more affordable prices and were selling like mad.  I am still trying to determine whether they were pulling my leg, or somehow misinformed.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>During the mid 80's quite a few Fiero's were converted to V8's by the GM Fiero Team, using the Gary Zumalt Conversion Kit. At that time all Fiero work was contracted to a company called ENTECH, which GM assigned Engineers to, to oversee the project. The conversion Fiero's were keep very hush, hush, and were tested at both the GM Milford and Arizona Proving Grounds. These cars were outperforming the Corvettes so badly that the Corvette Group made a very big stink about Pontiac even thinking of producing the car.  To make this story short, Corvette got their way, and all cars were destroyed. I don't think Pontiac has even one left in the proto car warehouse!!!  The car that started this string is an obvious prototype made outside GM, was probably an exercise that GM awarded to an outside shop, which they do once in a while to get new ideas.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||09-02-2001||01:35 PM||||[/b][/QUOTE]<BR>The car that started this string is an obvious prototype made outside GM, was probably an exercise that GM awarded to an outside shop, which they do once in a while to get new ideas.<P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P>Kind of like they did with the Asstek?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||California Kid||09-02-2001||01:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cooter:<BR><B>[/b]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>The car that started this string is an obvious prototype made outside GM, was probably an exercise that GM awarded to an outside shop, which they do once in a while to get new ideas.<P></B>[/QUOTE]<P>Kind of like they did with the Asstek?[/B][/QUOTE]<BR>Actually that one was done inside GM, the one done by styling looked real good, but they "de-contented" it so bad to take cost out, it turned out like sh!*<P>||||reg||6
